{
  "name": "Fill empty days in your social media calendar and catch failed posts with SocialRobot and OpenAI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Fill empty days in your social media calendar\n\nKeeps your SocialRobot calendar from going quiet. Each morning it looks a week ahead, writes a post for every day that has nothing scheduled, and tells you about posts that failed to publish.\n\n### How it works\n1. Every day at 7am the workflow lists the next 7 days, skipping the weekdays you exclude.\n2. It asks SocialRobot which of those days already have scheduled posts.\n3. For each empty day, OpenAI writes a short post from a rotating content pillar in your brand voice.\n4. SocialRobot schedules that post on Bluesky, Mastodon and Threads at your chosen time.\n5. In parallel, it emails you about newly failed posts, once per post.\n\n### Setup steps\n- [ ] Install the SocialRobot community node and add an API key from socialrobot.io/scheduler/api-keys\n- [ ] Pick an account in each **Schedule on** node\n- [ ] Add OpenAI and Gmail credentials and your email in **Email Failure Alert**\n- [ ] Edit pillars, brand, voice, time and language in **Set Calendar Options**\n\n### Customization\n- Plug in the optional Facebook or X node (X needs SocialRobot Pro).\n- Use the optional Slack node instead of email.\n- Set the Platform filter in **Get Scheduled Posts per Day** to check one network only.\n\nScheduled posts can be edited, rescheduled or deleted in SocialRobot before they go live.",
        "width": 480,
        "height": 912
      },
      "id": "cc8a5947-8246-432d-a27c-7a50922ebe07",
      "name": "Template Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
